    "created_at": "2015-12-23T19:05:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2015-12-23T19:05:47Z",
    "body": "Regarding the content security model: the algorithm for transferring an ImageBitmap simply copies the value of the origin-clean flag. So no tainting happens when the ImageBitmap is tranferred to a cross-origin script.  I am pretty sure this is the right thing to do, but I wanted to point this out because it is a bit tricky and I would like to make sure the security implications are considered by those who review this.\n",
